156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Evaluation of Research Quality. The Evaluation of Research Quality \(VQR\) is a comprehensive exercise conducted by ANVUR every five years. Its purpose is to evaluate the research and societal impact outcomes of public and private universities, research institutes, and private institutions that voluntarily participate. The assessment is carried out through a peer review process, where groups of experts evaluate research products. Bibliometric indicators may also be used when appropriate for the evaluation of publications. In addition, the evaluation includes the assessment of selected projects related to knowledge transfer activities. The most recent evaluation \(VQR 2015-19\) involved the assessment of over 180,000 research products by a panel of over 650 selected experts and 11,000 external national and international reviewers. Additionally, 676 case studies related to knowledge transfer activities were evaluated by a mixed panel composed of experts from academia, professions, and civil society. The new evaluation exercise concerning the period 2020-2024 \(VQR 2020-2024\) has been started at the end of 2023 and will be completed by June 2026. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
