162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Initial and Periodic Accreditation of Academic institutions and their study programmes, including PhD Programmes. ANVUR is also in charge of the initial and periodic evaluation of teaching, research and internationalisation activities of Italian universities. Evaluation concerns the strategic planning and procedures put in place to enhance the quality of research and teaching activities, and their human resources management practices. Initial and periodic accreditation of PhD programmes involves a comprehensive evaluation process to ensure that these programs meet established standards of quality and excellence. Initial accreditation assesses new PhD programs to verify they have the necessary resources, faculty, curriculum, and infrastructure to provide a high-quality educational experience. Periodic accreditation, on the other hand, involves regular reviews of existing PhD programmes to ensure they continue to meet these standards and are effectively contributing to academic and professional fields. This process typically includes self-assessment reports, site visits, and evaluations by external experts. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
