/P 481 0 R
/ActualText (VQR. In the first and second Evaluation of Research Quality exercise, and, partly, also in the third one \(VQR 2015-19\), a combination of citations and journal indicators was used to pre-assign any given research output to a specific class of merit. In the new VQR 2020-24, ANVUR continues to promote a responsible use of bibliometric indicators, merely as a tool to support qualitative evaluation, placing greater emphasis  on the role of peer review also in bibliometric areas. Furthermore, the number of scientific products per researcher required has been reduced from 3 to 2.5, as part of a gradual shift towards placing a higher emphasis on quality rather than quantity.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
